I'll add a loading skeleton to the Chat component that displays when the chat is loading. This will improve UX by showing a placeholder while data is being fetched.

**Changes needed:**
1. Add a computed property to detect if chat is loading
2. Add a skeleton loader component template
3. Show skeleton when loading, hide normal content

```vue src/components/chat/Chat.vue
<script setup>
import CheckLists from './CheckLists.vue'
import PRChangesPanel from '@/components/vibe/panels/PRChangesPanel.vue'
import ChatFileList from './ChatFileList.vue'
